# continuity — a body fallen, and the phase carries on
#
# The brewer is slain where he stands. The party has not moved and the hour has not passed, so the
# CONTINUE does not close the phase (NarrativeController.ContinueNarrationSegment). What left is
# greyed: both slay buttons (the bare one, never pressed, can no longer be done either) and the
# brewer's keyword. What came is observed at once, in a block added to the live text: the body, and
# what he carried beside it.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --grant-item knife --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Hall" --period dawn --observe-only "brewer"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy succeed
goal slay
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 1
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 1
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect SUCCESS
expect Slain:

click button
wait
advance 12 180
state
regions
expect-not after trying to
expect-state actions action 0 verb=slay state=spent
expect-state actions action 1 verb=slay state=spent
expect-state pois Remains
quit
